1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
2	"""
3	TickTick MCP Server - Comprehensive Task Management Integration.
4	
5	This MCP server provides a complete interface for interacting with TickTick,
6	combining both V1 (OAuth2) and V2 (Session) APIs for maximum functionality.
7	It enables AI assistants to manage tasks, projects, tags, and track productivity.
8	
9	=== CAPABILITIES ===
10	
11	Task Management:
12	    - Create tasks with titles, due dates, priorities, tags, reminders, and recurrence
13	    - Create subtasks (parent-child relationships)
14	    - Update, complete, delete, and move tasks between projects
15	    - List active, completed, and overdue tasks
16	    - Search tasks by title or content
17	
18	Project Management:
19	    - Create, read, update, and delete projects
20	    - Organize projects into folders
21	    - Get project details with all tasks
22	
23	Tag Management:
24	    - Create, rename, merge, and delete tags
25	    - Tags support hierarchical nesting
26	    - Apply tags to tasks for organization
27	
28	User Information:
29	    - Get user profile and account status
30	    - Access productivity statistics (completion rates, scores, levels)
31	    - Track focus/pomodoro sessions
32	
33	=== TICKTICK API BEHAVIORS ===
34	
35	IMPORTANT: TickTick has several unique API behaviors that tools account for:
36	
37	1. SOFT DELETE: Deleting tasks moves them to trash (deleted=1) rather than
38	   permanently removing them. Deleted tasks remain accessible via get_task.
39	
40	2. RECURRENCE REQUIRES START_DATE: Creating recurring tasks without a start_date
41	   silently ignores the recurrence rule. Always provide start_date with recurrence.
42	
43	3. PARENT-CHILD RELATIONSHIPS: Setting parent_id during task creation is ignored
44	   by the API. Use the make_subtask tool to establish parent-child relationships.
45	
46	4. DATE CLEARING: To clear a task's due_date or start_date, you must also clear
47	   both dates together (TickTick restores due_date from start_date otherwise).
48	
49	5. TAG ORDER: The API does not preserve tag order - tags may be returned in
50	   any order regardless of how they were provided.
51	
52	6. INBOX: The inbox is a special project that cannot be deleted. Its ID is
53	   available via get_status (inbox_id field).
54	
55	=== AUTHENTICATION ===
56	
57	This server requires BOTH V1 and V2 authentication for full functionality:
58	
59	V1 (OAuth2) - Required for get_project_with_data:
60	    TICKTICK_CLIENT_ID      - OAuth2 client ID from developer portal
61	    TICKTICK_CLIENT_SECRET  - OAuth2 client secret
62	    TICKTICK_ACCESS_TOKEN   - Access token from OAuth2 flow
63	
64	V2 (Session) - Required for most operations:
65	    TICKTICK_USERNAME       - TickTick account email
66	    TICKTICK_PASSWORD       - TickTick account password
67	
68	Optional:
69	    TICKTICK_REDIRECT_URI   - OAuth2 redirect URI (default: http://localhost:8080/callback)
70	    TICKTICK_TIMEOUT        - Request timeout in seconds (default: 30)
71	    TICKTICK_DEVICE_ID      - Device identifier (auto-generated if not set)
72	
73	=== RESPONSE FORMATS ===
74	
75	All tools support two response formats via the `response_format` parameter:
76	
77	- "markdown" (default): Human-readable formatted text with headers, lists, and
78	  timestamps in readable format. Best for displaying results to users.
79	
80	- "json": Machine-readable structured data with all available fields.
81	  Best for programmatic processing or when specific field values are needed.
82	
83	=== ERROR HANDLING ===
84	
85	Tools return clear, actionable error messages:
86	- Authentication errors: Check credentials configuration
87	- Not found errors: Verify resource ID exists
88	- Validation errors: Check input parameters
89	- Rate limit errors: Wait before retrying
90	- Server errors: Retry or contact support
91	"""
