## 3. Environment variables / config options that can disable/skip embedding model loading

**There is NO environment variable or config option to skip or disable embedding model loading.** The loading is unconditional.

The evidence:

- **`VectorStore.__init__`** (lines 71-83 in `vector_store.py`) always calls `_init_chromadb()` then `_init_embedding_model()`. There is no conditional guard.
- **`VectorStoreConfig`** in `config.py` (lines 15-35) has fields `backend`, `embedding_model`, `collection_name`, `persist_directory` -- but no flag like `enabled` or `skip_embeddings`.
- **`MCPSkillsConfig`** (lines 311-472 in `config.py`) has no top-level flag to skip vector store initialization either.
- **`IndexingEngine.__init__`** (engine.py, lines 105-195) always creates `VectorStore` unconditionally; there is no `vector_backend="none"` or similar check.
- Grep for `SKIP`, `DISABLE`, `environ`, `getenv` across the indexing/vector_store code returned no results. The only env var used in the project is `TOKENIZERS_PARALLELISM` (set in `cli/main.py` line 11) and `MCP_SKILLSET_DEBUG` (line 16).

The only way to avoid loading the embedding model would be to modify the code -- for example, by adding a new config flag and conditional logic in `VectorStore.__init__` or `IndexingEngine.__init__`.

Note: `VectorStoreConfig.backend` (line 25 in `config.py`) supports `"chromadb"`, `"qdrant"`, or `"faiss"`, but the `VectorStore` class itself does not check this field -- it always uses ChromaDB with sentence-transformers.

